  "id": "Compound::DB00687 - Gene::2908",
  "verbalization": "Fludrocortisone, a synthetic glucocorticoid, is linked to Nr3c1 through a series of mechanistic pathways that involve the binding of glucocorticoids to the glucocorticoid receptor (GR). The evidence suggests that Fludrocortisone, through its interaction with Prednisolone, which is a metabolite of Fludrocortisone, binds to Nr3c1. This binding is consistent across multiple paths, indicating a core mechanism of glucocorticoid receptor activation. The presence of a common ancestor, Therapeutic Glucocorticoid, and the 3-Oxo-Delta(4) Steroid class further supports the biological relevance of this interaction. The observed effects, such as alkalosis hypokalaemia and increased insulin requirement, are mediated by the GR, which is a well-established target of glucocorticoids. The integration of these pathways highlights the role of Nr3c1 in the physiological response to glucocorticoids, with Fludrocortisone acting as a precursor in the signaling cascade. The evidence is robust and consistent, reinforcing the mechanistic link between Fludrocortisone and Nr3c1.",
